agile_ict/static/images/* ```

#### Step B: Disable Branch Protection (On the Web)
1.  Go to your repo on **GitHub.com**.
2.  Click **Settings** (top tab).
3.  Click **Branches** (left sidebar).
4.  If you see a "Branch protection rule" for `main`, click **Delete** or **Edit**.
5.  If you edit it, scroll down and check **"Allow force pushes."** Click Save.



#### Step C: The "Clean" Push
Now, let's run the command in PowerShell using the "Token-in-URL" method which bypasses Windows' confused memory.

```powershell
# 1. Clean out any old remote settings
git remote remove origin

# 2. Add it back fresh
git remote add origin https://github.com/freddyoung/agile_ict.git

# 3. Force push using the token directly in the URL
# (Replace [TOKEN] with your ghp_... string)
git push https://freddyoung:[TOKEN]@github.com/freddyoung/agile_ict.git main --force